Guix build sandbox workaround: redirect ghostty's uucode Zig URL dependency
to a local path so the build does not require network access.  Since the
0c2a290d pin, the libvt build graph eagerly resolves three more URL
dependencies:
- pkg/translate-c (new wrapper package) vendors vancluever/translate-c,
  which in turn vendors arocc; the wrapper's top-level
  @import("translate_c") requires the dependency to resolve locally at
  build-graph construction time.
- pkg/wuffs (now wired into libvt for kitty graphics) vendors google/wuffs
  and pixels; its build.zig lazyDependency calls run while the build graph
  is constructed.
The package definition populates deps/translate-c, deps/aro, deps/wuffs
and deps/pixels from Guix origins; these hunks rewrite the URL
dependencies to those local paths.
Regenerated against ghostty commit 0c2a290d3a3e2a599be3a43435d778a5896667ee.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Guix-specific build environment]

